 { The worst case scenario you could find yourself in is when the passive piece is a very high value one, and when it is permanently out of the game. Such situations are rare, but generally fatal. In the current position, unfortunately for Black they find themselves in exactly this spot. } 1. { -KEY- } Qxb2 $18 { With the Black queen stuck on h4, the extra pawn that Black has is irrelevant. } Rf3 { Black makes a desperate attempt to break the lock. } 2. Qb1 $1 { A beautiful solution! White ignores the rook and repositions the queen to eye g6 against the possibility of ...Rxg3. } ( { Black was hoping that they would get to muddy the waters after } 2. gxf3 gxf3 { when White remains winning, but the game gets messy as White has to play Kf1 and start running with their king. } ) 
Rbf8 { Threatening ...Rxf2. } ( 2... Rxg3 { This move will not save Black: } 3. Qg6 $1 Kh8 4. fxg3 Qxg3 5. Qxh6 Kg8 6. Qxg5 { While Black's queen continues to struggle, now the even bigger problem is Black's king safety: } Kh8 7. Rc4 $18 { Mate will soon follow, with one idea being to play Qh5+ followed by Rxg4+. } ) 
3. gxf3 { Now capturing is a different story, since White is ready to attack immediately. } gxf3 4. Qg6+ Kh8 5. Qf7 $3 { There were a few ways to win, but to my eyes this is the most beautiful. } ( 5. Qh5 { Having won a clean rook, White could simply force off the queens and win the endgame. However, they choose a more spectacular finish. } ) 
Rxf7 6. exf7 Kg7 { Black's king has to step on to g7 to prevent the pawn from promoting, but now White wins back the queen. } 7. Nf5+ { This was White's clever idea. } Kxf7 8. Nxh4 $18 { White has two rooks for just a knight, with an easily winning position. While some of the tactical ideas were quite flashy, the major element at play was positional in nature. Black's queen was paralysed, and since this was a permanent problem, the position could not be saved. Piece paralysis is a recurring theme in chess. While it tends to happen mostly to a single piece, it can also happen to the entire configuration. Let's take a look at a couple of examples of this. } 
