 { Black to play. Can you find the strongest 2-move piece maneuver? } 18... { -KEY- } Ne8 $1 19. a4 Nd6 $17 { With this sequence, Black activates their knight and improves their position in several other ways: 1. White's strongest asset, the pawn on d5, is now blockaded. 2. Black can now think about pushing their 4 vs 3 kingside pawn majority. 3. White's pawn on c4 is permanently under fire, tying down White's pieces. } 20. a5 f5 $1 { Black has obtained an ideal arrangement, and the combination of the superior pawn structure and better placed pieces offers them considerable chances to press for the win from here as long as they contain White's counterplay on the queenside. } 21. axb6 axb6 22. Ra7 Nf6 23. Ra6 Rb8 $17 { With the queenside under control, Black is ready to march the pawns forward as well as perhaps centralise their king in the future. White will struggle to hold the position. This brings us to a close for the first section. Next up, we'll turn to the topic of piece exchanges, see you there! } 
